#
# CardDemo migration | services/common-lib/src/main/resources/META-INF/spring.factories
#
# Purpose: registers the startup contract the shared kernel enforces before any service context
#       refreshes -- the check that every environment-variable placeholder the active configuration
#       reads can actually be resolved -- so that a deployment missing a variable is refused with that
#       variable's name instead of failing later in a component that has never heard of it.
#
# WHY : Assumptions: an environment post-processor is discovered through THIS file and not through the
#       META-INF/spring/*.imports mechanism beside it. The .imports form is read by
#       ImportCandidates and serves auto-configuration classes only; Spring Boot 4.1 loads
#       environment post-processors in SpringFactoriesEnvironmentPostProcessorsFactory, which calls
#       SpringFactoriesLoader.load(org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor.class, ...) --
#       and SpringFactoriesLoader reads META-INF/spring.factories. A registration written in the
#       .imports style would be a file nothing reads, so the check would be compiled, tested and never
#       invoked, which is the silent failure mode the sibling imports file was itself written to cure.
#
# WHY : Assumptions: the key is the CURRENT interface, org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor.
#       Spring Boot 4.1 still loads the deprecated org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor
#       key for compatibility, so both spellings work today; naming the deprecated one would tie this
#       registration to a removal already announced.
#
# WHY : Trade-offs: this is the second registration resource the module carries, where its charters
#       describe a library as something that contributes types rather than resources. The departure is
#       accepted for the same reason the auto-configuration import was: there is no mechanism by which
#       a library contributes a startup check to a consumer that has not been told to look for one, and
#       a check each service had to remember to declare is a check a service can omit -- which is
#       exactly how eight services came to share one unnamed failure.
#
org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
com.carddemo.common.config.RequiredEnvironmentVariablePostProcessor
